Z||000000||loafer87gt||07-10-2001||12:26 AM||||I can't believe we haven't had a single rainstorm yet this year. I was back at my folks farm up in Northern Saskatchewan last weekend, and the farmers have totally given up on their crops, some are even starting to plow them up. Its pretty sad, the canola field is about 1 foot high and the peas are even worse. Is it just our province or has anyone else been suffering from this drought? This reinforces my opinion of farming in general: its way too risky. There can be a lot of money made if everything goes according to plan, but there are way too many factors out of our control (ie. mother nature) that I could simply not risk it.||||reg||1
